<http://data.silknow.org/object/6b2c8f87-6285-3f36-a96e-f33be6cc83da/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Shawl of printed silk and wool gauze woven with additional stripes and bands of white silk at intervals, forming open checks. It is printed with a four to five inch border in deep maroon filled with flowers and hatched 'shawl flower' motifs. The field is filled with broad 6.5 inch stripes in white, green and pink containing well-spaced angled fat 'cones'. Across the stripes are printed cut flowers and a lattice of hatched 'shawl flowers'. The colours are green, yellow, blue and purple."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6b2c8f87-6285-3f36-a96e-f33be6cc83da> .

